# secrets — per-service pass-entry manifest for the spotify-mcp container
# (ADR-0016). Distinct from the root `secrets` manifest (RH-ADR-0009, which holds
# container-wide provider keys interpolated into compose as ENV vars): the
# Spotify secret is a JSON config FILE (clientId / clientSecret / redirectUri +
# OAuth tokens), not an ENV var. `just spotify-config` (scripts/deliver-config.sh)
# reads this manifest, runs `pass show` per line, and writes each value to its
# dest under spotify-mcp/.appdata (bind-mounted into the container at /data).
# Values never touch the repo; only these non-secret pass entry paths + dest
# paths are committed. This mirrors the per-profile secrets pattern
# (profiles/<profile>/secrets, ADR-0012).
#
# `#` comments and blank lines are ignored. Format: <pass entry path>  <dest>.
# Dest is relative to spotify-mcp/.
#
# First-time setup (one-time): on a machine WITH a browser (your laptop), run
# the upstream OAuth flow to populate the tokens, then store the whole
# spotify-config.json as a single pass entry (see spotify-mcp/README.md
# §Prerequisites):
#   pass insert royal-household/spotify-mcp/spotify-config.json
# then on home-k12:
#   just spotify-config

royal-household/spotify-mcp/spotify-config.json  .appdata/spotify-config.json